.policy "ruff-pt002-pytest-fixture-positional-args" revision 2
.description "Pass pytest fixture configuration such as scope or params as keyword arguments, not positionally, for clarity."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PT002 (flake8-pytest-style): a fixture decorator given positional arguments; pytest's own signature makes
// them keyword-only in recent versions. Only a function's first fixture decorator is read.
//   @pytest.fixture("module")            ← PT002
//   @pytest.fixture(scope="module")      not reported
#include "python/pytest.rr"
//   pytest_fixture(f, d, e), exc_item(c, a, j)

.violation PT002(at: node, f: symbol) code "PT002"
    "Pass the arguments of `{f}(...)` by keyword: positional ones map, in order, to `scope`, `params`, `autouse`, `ids` and `name`."
    suppress ruff "PT002"
PT002(d, x) :- pytest_fixture(_, d, e), exc_item(e, _, _), field(e, "function", g), text(g, x).
